I follow the rule that all the suicidal types -- gas spores, yellow
lights, etc. -- get taken out with projectiles before they can get
near me.  I'll throw anything I have at them: daggers, darts, rocks,
spellbooks, orcish helms, whatever.

If possible, I try to take them out while they're still away from my
pet, too; but if not, well, too bad.  In the end, pets can always be
replaced.  If the suicide trooper is already next to your pet, there's
usually not much hope (without a magic whistle) of getting them apart
before the situation, so to speak, blows up.

The most annoying thing about exploding critters, though, is that they
wake up nearby monsters.  This can be *really* annoying when you're in
the middle of a throne room, trying to sneak your way between a pair
of sleeping dragons, when suddenly a yellow light shows up.

